From 65971aaab67c2b017cf80ed7885b1cabdfc87263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:11:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/28] feat: implement VK_EXT_mesh_shader on Metal mesh
 pipelines

Problem: No mesh shaders: vkd3d-proton could not report D3D12 mesh shader tier 1.

Root cause: MoltenVK did not implement VK_EXT_mesh_shader, although Metal 3 GPUs (M1 included) have object/mesh stages.

Fix: Advertise taskShader/meshShader on Metal 3 GPUs (macOS 13+) with limits from Metal's mesh pipeline. Task and mesh shaders use the tessellation control/evaluation slots (a pipeline is never both) with bindings aliased to the TaskEXT/MeshEXT execution models; new Object/Mesh encoder stages. Pipelines are built as MTLMeshRenderPipelineDescriptor, the fragment stage on a scratch render descriptor, with an empty fragment function when Vulkan has none. vkCmdDrawMeshTasks{,Indirect,IndirectCount}EXT map to drawMeshThreadgroups{,WithIndirectBuffer}; the count variant reuses the indirect-count conversion kernel (reads 4 bytes past the last 12-byte command). Mesh pipelines have no vertex input state.

Verified by: test_mesh_shader_rendering 260/260, test_amplification_shader 57/57, test_mesh_shader_execute_indirect 136/136, test_mesh_shader_create_pipeline 11 pass (+1 upstream todo); native harness (meshtest) with Metal validation clean.

Off switch: none
